1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:07,315
Machine & tools holds the tool table: every cutter and drill on the N-200, by number.

2
00:00:07,315 --> 00:00:11,207
For now it is placeholder data. The amber box lists every value still to configure.

3
00:00:11,207 --> 00:00:15,882
The tool table: number, type, diameter, max depth and more for each tool.

4
00:00:15,882 --> 00:00:19,499
The Goldberg job needs a 6 mm drill for the Blum slide holes. Switch to millimetres to type it exactly.

5
00:00:19,499 --> 00:00:23,639
Add tool puts a new row at the bottom. Double-click a cell to change it.

6
00:00:23,639 --> 00:00:36,999
Type: drill-vertical. A description. Diameter 6 mm, max depth 30 mm.

7
00:00:36,999 --> 00:00:43,211
Save. Drills are matched by exact diameter, so the 6 mm holes will now find this drill.

8
00:00:43,211 --> 00:00:52,915
Back on the Goldberg job’s Output tab: 0 errors now.

9
00:00:52,915 --> 00:00:58,983
Tick the simulate box, and the MPR programs can be exported.

10
00:00:58,983 --> 00:01:03,118
The tools are still placeholders, though: load the real N-200 table and simulate before cutting.
